 "notes": "Output-only task. The four accepted C++ (3746090, 3746199, 3746210, 5032793; 3746210 and 5032793 are byte-identical) print stored networks for official files 4-8 and otherwise run a degree-checked greedy Kruskal that asserts it spans, so they abort on valid networks with tight bounds (4 of 40 generated inputs) and answer nothing else; they are no reference and their files are gone. orig.cpp: greedy Kruskal under the bounds on noisy weights with exchange repairs and single-swap local search, restarted, then simulated annealing with over-full people penalised; it matches the statement sample (24) and comes within 2% of the stored official networks. checker.py accepts any valid network at least as comfortable. Bounds on N, M and c come from the official party1-10.in (N <= 1000, M <= 20000), since the statement bounds only k."
